From: Sean Duncan <sean.duncan@datadoghq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fuse: disable export ops without export support

Ported to v6.12.115 from the Datadog 6.8.x patch of the same name
(DataDog/kata-containers#131). The guest kernel moved from 6.8 to 6.12
in DataDog/kata-containers#140 without this patch.

virtiofsd assigns FUSE node IDs in the order files are accessed, so the
IDs are only valid for the lifetime of one virtiofsd process. virtiofsd
does not set FUSE_EXPORT_SUPPORT.

FUSE still installs full export operations when the server does not
claim export support. overlayfs therefore treats a virtiofs lower layer
as able to decode file handles. It records trusted.overlay.origin with
the temporary node ID on copy-up, and follows it on lookup. With a Kata
rootfs-upper volume, the upper layer is snapshotted and restored into a
new VM with a new virtiofsd. The stored node ID then resolves to an
unrelated cached inode, and open() returns ESTALE.

Upstream commit e022f6a1c711 ("fuse: add support for explicit export
disabling", v6.9) installs encode-only export operations only when the
server sends FUSE_NO_EXPORT_SUPPORT. virtiofsd 1.14 never sends that
flag, so v6.12 still has the problem.

Install encode-only export operations whenever the server does not
claim export support, and reject file handle decoding in that case even
for inodes that are in the cache. overlayfs then stops recording origin
file handles and ignores origin xattrs on existing upper layers.

Submounts already inherit s_export_op from the parent super block in
v6.12, so no change is needed there.

---
 fs/fuse/inode.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/fuse/inode.c b/fs/fuse/inode.c
--- a/fs/fuse/inode.c
+++ b/fs/fuse/inode.c
@@ -1045,16 +1045,13 @@
 	struct dentry *entry;
 	int err = -ESTALE;
 
-	if (handle->nodeid == 0)
+	if (handle->nodeid == 0 || !fc->export_support)
 		goto out_err;
 
 	inode = ilookup5(sb, handle->nodeid, fuse_inode_eq, &handle->nodeid);
 	if (!inode) {
 		struct fuse_entry_out outarg;
 		const struct qstr name = QSTR_INIT(".", 1);
-
-		if (!fc->export_support)
-			goto out_err;
 
 		err = fuse_lookup_name(sb, handle->nodeid, &name, &outarg,
 				       &inode);
@@ -1394,6 +1391,14 @@
 		fc->max_write = arg->minor < 5 ? 4096 : arg->max_write;
 		fc->max_write = max_t(unsigned, 4096, fc->max_write);
 		fc->conn_init = 1;
+		/*
+		 * Without FUSE_EXPORT_SUPPORT the server's node IDs are not
+		 * persistent. Expose encode-only export ops so overlayfs does
+		 * not record or follow origin file handles that can resolve to
+		 * an unrelated inode after the server restarts.
+		 */
+		if (!fc->export_support)
+			fm->sb->s_export_op = &fuse_export_fid_operations;
 	}
 	kfree(ia);
 
